nous portrait of female friendship against the heady atmosphere of modern Mumbai.  </p><p style=\"margin-left:0px;\">Nurse Prabha’s routine is troubled when she receives an unexpected gift from her estranged husband. Meanwhile, her younger roommate, Anu, pursues a secret relationship that defies her family's expectations. Away from the bustle of the metropolis, whilst on a trip to a beach town, Kapadia captures the radiance of young love. Prabha, Anu, and their coworker Parvaty confront heartache and hope, revealing the richness of sisterhood.  </p></div><!--]--><!--]--></div><!----></div><!----><aside class=\"matter matter--solid\"><div class=\"stack-deep matter__section\"><div class=\"richtext richtext--sm\"><p><strong>Payal Kapadia</strong> is a Mumbai-based filmmaker. She studied Film Direction at the Film &amp; Television Institute of India. Her short films <i>Afternoon Clouds</i> and <i>And What Is The Summer Saying </i>premiered respectively at the Cinéfondation and the Berlinale. Her first feature film <i>A Night of Knowing Nothing</i> premiered at 2021 Director’s Fortnight, where it won the Golden Eye for best documentary.  </p></div></div></aside><!----><div class=\"target\"><div class=\"tt-widget\"><div class=\"tt-widget-fallback stack\"><a href=\"https://tickets.ibraaz.org/events/ibraaz/2346963/select-date?ref=website_widget\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"title\"> Click here to buy tickets </a><a href=\"https://www.tickettailor.com?rf=wdg_265722\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"tt-widget-powered\"> Sell tickets online with Ticket Tailor </a></div></div></div><!----></div></div><!----><span></span></main><footer class=\"footer\"><div class=\"footer__grid\"><div class=\"stack-deep footer__cta\"><div class=\"details\"><h2 class=\"rubric rubric--sm rubric--compact\">Culture is a work in progress. Stay updated.</h2><button class=\"details__btn btn\"><span class=\"line\">Subscribe to our newsletter</span><svg vie