023L1.30323 3.12235L1.24853 3.05985L1.19393 3.1555H1.13923L1.08453 3.09678L1.02983 3.06269L0.97513 3.0731L0.92043 3.12235L0.86573 3.06553L0.81103 3.10909L0.756431 3.16307L0.70173 3.16118L0.64703 3.16212L0.59233 3.09962L0.53763 3.12898L0.48193 3.11951L0.42733 3.08542L0.37263 3.07216L0.28183 3.14697L0.31503 3.05891L0.30323 3.00683L0.36773 2.95379L0.33743 2.90076L0.35993 2.84773L0.34233 2.7947L0.36673 2.74167L0.30813 2.68864L0.32573 2.63561L0.33253 2.58258L0.363831 2.52955L0.273931 2.47747L0.27303 2.42348L0.26423 2.3714L0.26123 2.31837L0.32183 2.26535L0.27203 2.21231L0.37353 2.15928L0.27593 2.1072L0.36773 2.05417L0.336431 2.00114L0.28963 1.94811L0.34233 1.89508L0.341331 1.84204L0.35113 1.78902L0.27303 1.73599L0.301331 1.68391L0.35693 1.63087L0.33253 1.57784L0.354031 1.52482L0.26913 1.47178L0.29743 1.41875L0.33943 1.36572L0.34033 1.3127L0.358931 1.25966V1.20663L0.35793 1.1536L0.35603 1.10058L0.291531 1.04754L0.30523 0.99451L0.29443 0.941477L0.33063 0.888454L0.34523 0.835421L0.32183 0.782388L0.27003 0.729356L0.29053 0.676333L0.306231 0.6233L0.314031 0.570267L0.33553 0.516294L0.27983 0.463261L0.26813 0.410228L0.32183 0.360987L0.37263 0.406437L0.426331 0.359097L0.48103 0.309855L0.53573 0.407387L0.59033 0.332575L0.64503 0.403606L0.69973 0.399814L0.75443 0.385608L0.809131 0.396022L0.863831 0.349622L0.91853 0.395082L0.97223 0.383717L1.02783 0.408338L1.08163 0.394132L1.13623 0.32121L1.19093 0.348672L1.24563 0.381817L1.30033 0.360037L1.35403 0.36667L1.40873 0.333526L1.46343 0.353414L1.51813 0.386558L1.57283 0.363829L1.62753 0.309855L1.68213 0.36762L1.73683 0.385608L1.79053 0.376143L1.84523 0.411179L1.89993 0.308905L1.95463 0.340158L2.00933 0.303223L2.06403 0.360037Z\"></path></svg></button><!--]--></div><!----></div><div class=\"split__main\"><div class=\"split-clean\"><div class=\"split-clean__head\"><!--[--><!--[--><div class=\"richtext richtext--sm\"><p>Meriem, Gigi, and Tina are the main protagonists in this sun-drenched coming-of-age film, set amid the sea air of La Goulette. The three friends make a pact that this summer will mark the start of their journey into sensuality, challenging familial and communal order. On the Mediterranean shore, Boughedir delivers a multigenerational comedy about solidarity and friendship among the Muslim, Jewish, and Sicilian Catholic communities of this port city.  </p></div><!--]--><!--]--></div><!----></div><!----><aside class=\"matter matter--solid\"><div class=\"stack-deep matter__section\"><div class=\"richtext richtext--sm\"><p><strong>Férid Boughedir</strong> was born in 1944 in Hammam Lif, Tunisia. He started his career in cinema as a film critic writing for Jeune Afrique, a Francophone pan-African weekly news magazine. His articles, books, and his two well-received documentaries on African and Arab cinemas, <i>Caméra d’Afrique</i> and <i>Caméra Arabe</i>, which were presented in official selection at the Cannes International Film Festival, respectively, in 1983 and 1987, sealed his reputation as a respected scholar of African cinema. Boughedir’s first feature,<i> Halfaouine: Child of the Terraces</i>, won the Golden Tanit, the grand prize of the Carthage Film Festival.</p></div></div></aside><!----><div class=\"target\"><div class=\"tt-widget\"><div class=\"tt-widget-fallback stack\"><a href=\"https://tickets.ibraaz.org/events/ibraaz/2348862/select-date?ref=website_widget\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"title\"> Click here to buy tickets </a><a href=\"https://www.tickettailor.com?rf=wdg_265722\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"tt-widget-powered\"> Sell tickets online with Ticket Tailor </a></div></div></div><!----></div></div><div class=\"slice slice--matte\"><div class=\"slice__head\"><h2 class=\"signboard\">Related</h2></div><ul class=\"slice__body\"><!--[--><!--]--></ul></div><span></span></main><footer class=\"footer\"><div class=\"footer__grid\"><div class=\"stack-deep footer__cta\"><div class=\"details\"><h2 class=\"rubric rubric--sm rubric-